{
  "_notes": "Structured mechanical grants for feats, so a character's ability scores/spellbook/known-spell count/saving-throw proficiencies can be computed from what a feat actually gives instead of trusting a freeform note. Verified against dnd5e.wikidot.com + aidedd.org 2026-09-02 (full PHB/XGE/TCE 2014-ruleset feat list — see engine/CHECKLIST.md Phase 7b for the session log). Every entry here has a matching src/data/published_features.json entry (category: 'feat') with full RAW text, and a matching engine/data/feature-catalog.json id.",

  "_schema": {
    "source": "Book this feat is from: 'Player's Handbook' | 'Xanathar's Guide to Everything' | \"Tasha's Cauldron of Everything\".",
    "prerequisite": "null, or one of: {type:'ability_score', ability, min} | {type:'any_of', options:[{ability,min},...]} (meet ANY one) | {type:'genus', genera:[...]} (meet ANY listed genus/subgenus string, matched loosely against character.genus/subgenus) | {type:'proficiency', proficiency:'light_armor'|'medium_armor'|'heavy_armor'|'martial_weapon'} | {type:'spellcasting'} (character.spellcasting_ability or pact_magic present). Enforced by engine/rules/featPrerequisites.js — see that file for exactly how each type is evaluated, including the deliberate 'unknown proficiency data is permissive' rule (most characters.json entries don't populate armor_proficiencies/weapon_proficiencies at all, so a hard 'not proficient' block would false-negative almost every real character).",
    "ability_score_increase": "{choice_of:[...abilities], amount} — same mechanism asiFeat.js already had for Fey Touched/Shadow Touched. choice_of.length===1 auto-applies with no dropdown.",
    "grants_spells": "{fixed:[...names], choice:{count, level, schools}, casting_ability, free_cast_note} — same shape as Fey Touched/Shadow Touched, used both for known-spell-count verification (grants.js/isFeatGrantedSpell) and, new this pass, auto-applied to patch.spells by diffLevelUp when the level-up resolution supplies choices.spell_choice_1 etc.",
    "choices": "array of {id, label, type, count, options?} — a GENERIC extra-choice schema (beyond ability score) for feats that hand the player a pick. type is one of: 'skill' | 'tool' | 'skill_or_tool' | 'language' | 'damage_type' | 'weapon' | 'maneuver' | 'fighting_style' | 'class_list' | 'spell_text' (free-text spell name — see 7b note on why this isn't a full class-filtered spell-list dropdown) | 'text' (fully free, e.g. an Eldritch Invocation name). 'options' is a concrete array for the enumerable types; omitted for 'spell_text'/'text'. LevelUpTool.vue renders `count` pickers per choice, generically — no per-feat special-casing.",
    "stat_bonuses": "Copied verbatim onto the character's new feat feature entry when confirmed — same object shape src/utils/dnd_utils.js's resolveStats() already reads off character.features[].stat_bonuses for AC/saves/skills/passive perception/initiative. ONLY used for a flat, UNCONDITIONAL numeric bonus (e.g. Alert's +5 initiative, Observant's +5 passive Perception) — deliberately omitted for anything conditional on loadout/stance (Dual Wielder's +1 AC only while dual-wielding, Medium Armor Master's AC cap change) since the existing stat_bonuses mechanism has no notion of 'only when X' and adding it unconditionally would be a real correctness bug, not a discoverability win.",
    "grants_saving_throw_proficiency": "true only for Resilient — diffLevelUp adds the ability chosen via ability_score_increase.choice_of to patch.saving_throws.",
    "hp_bonus_per_level": "Tough only (2). Recorded for discoverability/tooltip text ONLY — deliberately NOT auto-applied to patch.hp_max. RAW is 'immediately +2× current level, then +2 more per level thereafter' — the retroactive lump sum on the level Tough is taken can't be expressed as a simple per-level-up delta without double-counting on every future level-up preview, and this project's existing scope boundary for feats (asiFeat.js's own comment) already draws the line at ability scores + known-spell counts for auto-application. Flagged, not guessed at."
  },

